====Verb====
{{sv-verb-reg}}

# {{lb|sv|intransitive}} to [[wake up]] (become awake – compare {{m|sv|väcka}})
#* {{quote-song|sv|year=1996|author={{w|Drängarna}} [The Farmhands]|album={{w|lang=sv|Fint vettö}} [{{l|sv|vettu}}]|trans-album=Nice Y'know|title=Kung över ängarna|trans-title=King of [over] the Meadows|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UlcFueNNpMY|text=Jag lägger mig i gräset ner. Ligger still och bara {{l|sv|ler}}. {{l|sv|slumrar|Slumrar}} {{l|sv|till|id=sudden and brief}} och {{l|sv|snarkar}} tyst. Drömmer om en kvinnas {{l|sv|byst}}. Då ser jag nån som emot mig går, {{l|sv|liderlig}} med {{l|sv|utsläppt}} hår. Hon är {{l|sv|vacker som en dag}}. I samma stund {{l|sv|så|id=adverbial filler}} '''vaknar''' jag. {{l|sv|svär|Svär}} [bit hard to make out the S] ett {{l|sv|tag}} men tänker sen: Hon kommer nog till mig inatt igen. Ännu lyser solen stark i skog och {{l|sv|mark|id=wild land}}.|t=I lie down in the grass ["Jag lägger mig ner i gräset" is the usual word order. {{m|sv|ner|Ner|down}} can be skipped]. [I] lie still and just grin [or smile]. [I] doze off and snore quietly. [I] dream of a woman's bosom. Then I see someone walking towards me ["Då ser jag nån som går emot mig" is the usual word order], lustful [in an unrestrained manner – old-fashioned – often used to imply "lecherous," but also more generally] with her hair let down [with out-released hair]. She is pretty as a picture ["beautiful as a day" – idiom]. At that moment [in the same moment] I '''wake up'''. [I] swear for a bit but then [I] think: She will probably come to me tonight again ["Igen inatt" is a more common word order in Swedish as well]. The sun still shines bright ["yet shines (V2 word order) the sun strong" – could be translated as "still the sun shines bright" to match, but sounds less awkward in Swedish] in woods and fields ["forest and (wild) land" – idiomatic]. [Could also be put in the present continuous. Matches the intuition in Swedish with the [I]s. See the usage notes for {{m|sv|-r}}.]}}
#: {{ux|sv|Har du '''vaknat''' på fel sida i dag?|Did you '''wake up''' on the wrong side today? [Are you in a bad mood for some reason? – idiomatic]}}
#: {{ux|sv|Jag '''vaknade''' med ett {{m|sv|ryck}}|I '''woke up''' with a start}}
#: {{ux|sv|Staden hade precis börjat '''vakna'''|The city was just starting to '''wake up'''}}

